# PSR-5f6a — finance recon edge (sub-slice)

Full `BG_FINANCE_RECON` is **five** files / **۲۵** call sites. This wave migrates
only the thin edge — gauges + job orchestration — and leaves detect / findings /
repair for follow-up sub-slices.

## Scope (exactly two files)

| File | Prior direct calls | Role |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `workspace-finance/finance-ops-metrics.ts` | 3 | scrape gauges (read-only counts) |
| `workspace-finance/recon/finance-recon-runner.ts` | 1 | auto-repair open-finding select |

Both use `getBackgroundAdminClient(BACKGROUND_ADMIN_REASON.BG_FINANCE_RECON)`.

## Explicitly deferred (same reason code)

| File | Calls | Planned wave |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `recon/findings-store.ts` | 6 | PSR-5f6b |
| `recon/repair-handlers.ts` | 4 | PSR-5f6c |
| `recon/detect.ts` | 11 | PSR-5f6d |

## Non-goals

- No gauge formula / lookback / auto-repair policy changes
- No detect SQL or repair handler mutation logic
- No integration / events clusters

## Ratchet after f6a

- f inventory: `migrated_file_count: 13`, `remaining_direct: 7`
- main: `api_src_admin_files: 13`, `api_src_admin_calls: 50`,
  `background_repair_direct_admin_files: 7`

